      "path": "SPEC.md",
      "content": "# Tiered pricing engine + ledger summary \u2014 build contract\n\nAll money values are integer cents. `Math.round` is applied only at the steps named below.\n\n## 1. Quantity tiers\n\n`tierFor(totalQuantity)` maps the summed order quantity to exactly one tier:\n\n| Quantity | Tier | Discount rate |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| >= 100 | platinum | 10% |\n| >= 50 and < 100 | gold | 5% |\n| < 50 | standard | 0% |\n\nBoundaries are inclusive on the lower edge: 50 is gold, 100 is platinum.\n\n## 2. Membership surcharge\n\n`account.membership` adds a surcharge rate applied AFTER the tier discount:\n\n| Membership | Rate |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| \"gold\" | 5% |\n| \"silver\" | 2% |\n| anything else (including missing) | 0% |\n\n## 3. Quote order of operations (exact)\n\n1. `subtotalCents` = sum of `priceCents * quantity` over all lines.\n2. `discountCents = Math.round(subtotalCents * discountRate)`.\n3. `discountedCents = subtotalCents - discountCents`.\n4. `surchargeCents = Math.round(discountedCents * surchargeRate)`.\n5. `totalCents = discountedCents + surchargeCents`.\n\nNo intermediate rounding. Validation: `items` non-empty array (else RangeError mentioning `items`); every line needs non-empty `sku`, integer `priceCents` >= 0, integer `quantity` >= 1 (else RangeError mentioning `line` and the offending index). `account` may be omitted (standard tier, 0% surcharge).\n\n## 4. Ledger summary module\n\n`data/ledger.ndjson` holds one JSON object per line: `{\"sku\": string, \"units\": integer, \"unitPriceCents\": integer}`, with a trailing newline. `summarize(lines)` takes already-parsed line objects and returns `{ perSku, totalUnits, totalRevenueCents }` where `perSku[sku] = { units, revenueCents }` and `revenueCents = units * unitPriceCents`. Empty `lines` throws RangeError mentioning `lines`. The module must not read the filesystem: the CLI caller reads `data/ledger.ndjson`, parses each JSON line (tolerating the trailing newline), and passes the objects in.\n\n## 5. Module boundaries\n\n- `src/tiers.mjs` exports `tierFor(quantity)` and `TIER_RATES`.\n- `src/pricing.mjs` imports thresholds from `src/tiers.mjs` (no duplicated constants).\n- `src/summary.mjs` exports `summarize(lines)` and must not import the pricing modules."
    },
